{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh brought near.</b> It should have been written וּפַרְעֹה קָרַב — what is הִקְרִיב? He brought himself near and took trouble to advance ahead of them, as he had stipulated with them." "<b>Traveled after them.</b> With one heart, like one man. Another matter — ״and behold, Egypt traveled after them״: they saw the prince of Egypt traveling from the heavens to help the Egyptians — Tanḥuma." "<b>And they cried out.</b> They seized the craft of their fathers — of Abraham it says ״to the place where he stood״ (Genesis 19), of Isaac ״to meditate in the field״ (Genesis 24), of Jacob ״and he encountered the place״ (Genesis 28)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:05.416634232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}